<% content_for :title, "Turbo Confirm" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">Utilities</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Turbo Confirm</h1>
  <p class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    Intercepts Turbo's native <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">confirm()</code> and replaces it with the kit's styled dialog — so <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-turbo-confirm</code> attributes just work.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 p-12 mb-8">
  <%# A plain data-turbo-confirm names no variant, so the dialog's own default applies: destructive. %>
  <%= link_to "Delete item", demo_delete_path,
      data: { turbo_method: :delete, turbo_confirm: "Delete this item? This cannot be undone." },
      class: "rounded-md bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white transition-colors" %>
  <%# Every part of the confirmation travels as data-turbo-confirm- plus the option key. %>
  <%= link_to "Publish post", demo_delete_path,
      data: {
        turbo_method: :delete,
        turbo_confirm: "Readers will see it immediately.",
        turbo_confirm_title: "Publish this post?",
        turbo_confirm_confirm_label: "Publish",
        turbo_confirm_confirm_variant: "default"
      },
      class: "rounded-md bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white hover:bg-neutral-700 dark:hover:bg-neutral-200 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white dark:text-neutral-900 transition-colors" %>
  <%# The same attributes on a real submit button, which is where Turbo looks first. %>
  <%= button_to "Archive project", demo_delete_path, method: :delete, id: "archive-submit",
      form: { data: { turbo_confirm_cancel_label: "Keep it" } },
      data: {
        turbo_confirm: "It stays available from a direct link.",
        turbo_confirm_title: "Archive this project?",
        turbo_confirm_confirm_label: "Archive",
        turbo_confirm_confirm_variant: "secondary"
      },
      class: "rounded-md bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 hover:bg-neutral-200 dark:hover:bg-neutral-700 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-colors" %>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Setup</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
  Mount the controller once in your layout alongside the confirm dialog singleton:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">Layout — ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#turbo-confirm-setup" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="turbo-confirm-setup" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_turbo_confirm_setup) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#turbo-confirm-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="turbo-confirm-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_turbo_confirm_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">How it works</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>Patches <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">Turbo.config.forms.confirm</code> in <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">connect()</code>.</li>
  <li>Reads <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-turbo-confirm-title</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">-confirm-label</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">-cancel-label</code> and <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">-confirm-variant</code> from the submit button, the form, or a <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">data-turbo-method</code> link.</li>
  <li>A confirmation that names no variant gets the dialog's rendered default — <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">:destructive</code>, unless your layout rendered otherwise. Nothing one confirmation sets leaks into the next.</li>
  <li>An icon or any other markup never travels through an attribute: render a dialog with the <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">icon</code> slot and open it with <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">customConfirmDialog</code>.</li>
  <li>Falls back to <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">window.defaultConfirmDialog()</code> if present, then to browser <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">confirm()</code>.</li>
  <li>Restores the original handler in <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">disconnect()</code>.</li>
</ul>
